- For each value in the integer array parameter `nums1`, find the index `j` in the integer array parameter `nums2` such that the value in `nums1` is equal to the value in `nums2` at index `j`.
- If there is a next greater element to the right of the value in `nums2` at index `j`, the corresponding value in the integer array result is the next greater element.
- If there is no next greater element to the right of the value in `nums2` at index `j`, the corresponding value in the integer array result is -1.
- The length of the integer array result is equal to the length of the integer array parameter `nums1`.
- All values in the integer array result are either the next greater element to the right or -1.